* comment_handling_regression.dts
* Proves the canonical DotTalk++ comment vocabulary is honored on the script path
* after the AIF-037 lexer consolidation (one shared dotscript_lexing module).
*
* Canonical full-line comments: *  REM   (+ tolerated #  //)
* Inline comments: && and # (cut to end of line); single & (macro) survives.
*
* Expected output is exactly three lines, in order:
*   COMMENT-REGRESSION-BEGIN
*   AFTER-COMMENT-LINES
*   COMMENT-REGRESSION-END
* Every comment line below must produce NO output.

FORMULA "COMMENT-REGRESSION-BEGIN"

REM this whole line is a comment
* and this one
// and this one
&& and this one
# and this one

FORMULA "AFTER-COMMENT-LINES"          && this trailing && comment is ignored

FORMULA "COMMENT-REGRESSION-END"       # this trailing # comment is ignored
